                <pb facs="0380" n="372" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg372"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.48/253</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-28T11:00:00-03:00">September 28, 1938—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 28—10:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>228. Notwithstanding the situation described in my 221, September 22, 1 p.m. the
                    Brazilian authorities have decided, solely because we are suggesting it, to
                    donate coffee for Spanish refugees. They want to know how much coffee is desired
                    and they hope that measures can be taken to insure that the coffee is actually
                    used for purposes indicated and none of it sold by the Spanish authorities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
